summary:
  A round button that cannot be pressed shows no tooltip.

history:
  The tip is often the only place that says why a button is switched off.
  The press area does not hover while the button is disabled, so the tip
  has a hover of its own.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CircleButton.qml

find:
          visible: tipHover.hovered && text.length > 0

replace:
          visible: pressArea.containsMouse && text.length > 0

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_buttontip.qml::test_a_button_that_is_switched_off_still_shows_its_tip.
